    <div class="cs-hero">
      <h1 class="cs-hero-title">Automate Java coding standards with Checkstyle</h1>
      <p class="cs-hero-tagline">
        Checkstyle analyzes Java source code against configurable rules for
        naming, imports, formatting, Javadoc, class design, and more. It helps
        teams enforce consistent coding standards automatically.
      </p>
      <p class="cs-hero-cta">
        <a class="cs-btn cs-btn-primary" href="getting_started.html">Get Started</a>
        <a class="cs-btn cs-btn-secondary" href="checks.html">Browse Checks</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <section name="">
    <subsection name="See Checkstyle in Action"
                  id="See_Checkstyle_in_Action">
      <p>
        Configure a rule, run Checkstyle against your Java source, and get a
        precise violation.
      </p>

      <div class="cs-workflow">
        <div class="cs-workflow-card">
          <p class="cs-workflow-title">1 - Configure</p>
          <div class="wrapper"><pre class="cs-workflow-code"><span class="cs-workflow-dim"><span class="cs-code-tag">&lt;?xml</span> <span class="cs-code-attribute">version</span>=<span class="cs-code-string">"1.0"</span><span class="cs-code-tag">?&gt;</span>
<span class="cs-code-tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE</span> <span class="cs-code-attribute">module</span> <span class="cs-code-attribute">PUBLIC</span> <span class="cs-code-string">"-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN"</span> <span class="cs-code-string">"https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd"</span><span class="cs-code-tag">&gt;</span>

<span class="cs-code-tag">&lt;module</span> <span class="cs-code-attribute">name</span>=<span class="cs-code-string">"Checker"</span><span class="cs-code-tag">&gt;</span>
  <span class="cs-code-tag">&lt;module</span> <span class="cs-code-attribute">name</span>=<span class="cs-code-string">"TreeWalker"</span><span class="cs-code-tag">&gt;</span></span>
    <span class="cs-workflow-em"><span class="cs-code-tag">&lt;module</span> <span class="cs-code-attribute">name</span>=<span class="cs-code-string">"AvoidStarImport"</span><span class="cs-code-tag">/&gt;</span></span>
  <span class="cs-workflow-dim"><span class="cs-code-tag">&lt;/module&gt;</span>
<span class="cs-code-tag">&lt;/module&gt;</span></span></pre></div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-workflow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

        <div class="cs-workflow-card">
          <p class="cs-workflow-title">2 - Your Java code</p>
          <div class="wrapper"><pre class="cs-workflow-code"><span class="cs-code-keyword">import</span> java.util.<span class="cs-workflow-em"><span class="cs-code-string">.*</span></span>;
<span class="cs-workflow-dim"><span class="cs-code-keyword">class</span> Test {
  List names;
}</span></pre></div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-workflow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

        <div class="cs-workflow-card">
          <p class="cs-workflow-title">3 - Run Checkstyle</p>
          <div class="wrapper"><pre class="cs-workflow-code"><span class="cs-workflow-dim">$ java -jar checkstyle-</span><span class="cs-code-number">${projectVersion}</span><span class="cs-workflow-dim">-all.jar
    -c config.xml Test.java</span>
<span class="cs-workflow-error">[ERROR]</span> Test.java:<span class="cs-code-number">1</span>:<span class="cs-code-number">1</span>: Using the '<span class="cs-workflow-em">.*</span>' form
    of import should be avoided - java.util.*.
    [AvoidStarImport]</pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Learn more about
        <a href="config.html">configuration</a> and
        <a href="running.html">running Checkstyle</a>.
      </p>
    </subsection>


